  "caption": "Quinn planked for five minutes every day for 90 days. The back still ached every morning, so the next plan was to plank even longer.\n\nKay explained that persistent back pain is often about timing, not weak abs: the deep stabilising muscles may switch on a little late. Long planks build endurance but may not retrain that quick timing.\n\nWhat can help: learning a gentle deep switch-on lying down, then carrying it into sitting, standing and stepping, adding load once it feels reliable, and varying your exercises.\n\nGet it checked if you have leg pain with numbness or tingling, foot weakness, bladder or bowel changes, or pain that is severe or getting worse.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
